On a single dataset, often very little of a standard representation varies. On hERG $K_i$, 1,815 of the 2,048 ECFP4 features take one value in at least 95\% of the 1,412 molecules (Section~\ref{sec:flaws:constant}). In addition, several representations give different molecules, mostly stereoisomers, the same feature vector, and no model can separate those molecules, whatever their labels. ECFP4 gives 56 of the 1,412 hERG $K_i$ molecules a vector shared with another molecule, all of them stereoisomers (``Molecules with identical feature vectors'').

A distance sums over every feature, so when only a few features matter for the property, the rest dominate the sum (Section~\ref{sec:flaws:similarity}). Across 70 combinations of dataset and representation, the Spearman correlation between pair distance and label difference was below 0.10 in 44.
