As explained above, a hybrid search returns a list of settings that function as a feature selection method to generate the hybrid representation itself. These settings are recorded in a blueprint that can be used on new folds of the same dataset or even new data. The blueprint contains additional information, including some fields for analysis, meta-data, and scores. These scores are used only for comparative purposes as in this research, the hybrids are rebuilt per-fold and are scored as such. 

