Additional file~\ref{app:add:blueprint_listing} lists every field of a blueprint and its type.

The blueprint does not record the specific features that are returned by the hybrid, as it is meant to be re-run using the same settings on new, labeled data. Alternatively, you can reuse the features of a labeled fit and apply them to data with no labels under the assumption that the same features matter between sets. 

The blueprint is extended by an additional explainability layer. Since it does not store feature names, this additional step runs on a completed hybrid, records where each selected feature came from and, wherever possible, what that feature means. An ECFP4 bit is named by the atom environment that sets it, written as a SMILES fragment from a molecule with the bit set. MACCS keys are named by their SMILES arbitrary target specification (SMARTS) pattern and a short name, and descriptor features by descriptor name. Protein composition, descriptor and k-mer features, antibody composition, one-hot, BLOSUM, structural and inverse-folding features and PCA components are named too. MAP4 and DRFP features get only a bit index, and Avalon, Mordred, atom-pair, graph-kernel and learned-embedding features only the representation name and dimension index.

\subsection{The search space}\label{sec:method:searchspace}
