\subsubsection{Pre-processing}
Additional file~\ref{app:datasets} gives the shared and per-dataset pre-processing steps, with the counts after each step. The LogD and Caco-2 labels are clipped at their 1st and 99th percentiles, so on Caco-2, for example, 22 molecules share the highest label and 23 the lowest.

% TODO: manual review
\subsubsection{Splitting rules}
As in Chapter~\ref{chap:robustness} (Section~\ref{sec:robustness:methods}), no group is split between folds, and classification folds are also stratified with a fixed seed. Every dataset uses five outer folds, and no split is random (Section~\ref{sec:evaluation}). On a given dataset, every representation, model and hybrid is scored on the same folds.

% TODO: manual review
\subsubsection{Groups by domain}
The small-molecule datasets, QM9 included, are grouped by Bemis--Murcko scaffold (Section~\ref{sec:robustness:methods}), here keeping stereochemistry. On QM9 the largest group is the empty scaffold of acyclic molecules, with 1,041 of the 9,978 molecules. % TODO: manual review
The two datasets from Biogen \citep{fang2023} (rat microsomal clearance and MDR1--MDCK efflux) have 1.2 and 1.1 molecules per scaffold, respectively, so holding out a scaffold there is close to holding out single molecules. Chapter~\ref{chap:robustness} used a different scaffold key and different curation for its versions of LogD, Caco-2, hERG $K_i$ and QM9, and Additional file~\ref{app:datasets:ch3} lists the differences.

% TODO: manual review
The reaction dataset is Buchwald--Hartwig C--N couplings from high-throughput plates. Following \citet{Ahneman2018}, it is grouped by additive: each held-out fold holds four or five additives unseen in training (Additional file~\ref{app:datasets}).

% TODO: manual review
In the Koenig deep mutational scan of the anti-vascular endothelial growth factor (VEGF) antibody G6, each variant carries one mutation. % TODO: manual review
Variants are grouped by their mutated position, giving 225 groups. With all mutations at one position on the same side of a split, a model cannot look up a per-position effect at test time \citep{Vieira2026}. The nanobody and humanness sets are grouped by single-linkage clusters at 95\% sequence identity, the identity threshold \citet{Kenlay2024} used to cluster their pretraining sequences.

% TODO: manual review
The two AbAgym deep mutational scans (EGFR and angiopoietin-2 binding) are grouped by mutated position, as for the Koenig scans, giving 36 and 20 groups. The $\Delta\Delta G$ set joins antibody--antigen entries from SKEMPI 2.0 and AB-Bind. It is grouped by protein complex, giving 30 groups, and hence no complex is on both sides of a split. The five Ginkgo developability assays are measured on the same panel of antibodies. Two are retention times, in hydrophobic interaction chromatography (HIC) and standup monolayer adsorption chromatography (SMAC). The others are affinity-capture self-interaction nanoparticle spectroscopy (AC-SINS), expression titer, and polyreactivity to Chinese hamster ovary (CHO) cell proteins. We use the five cross-validation folds released with the competition \citep{vanNiekerk2026} as the groups, which makes the outer folds the competition's own.

