Four comparisons run inside every held-out fold of the target: the best single representation, a hybrid searched on the target's training molecules as the upper reference, the source settings with features re-selected on the target, and the source's selected features applied unchanged. The last two ask separately whether the search decisions and the chosen features transfer. We use five folds grouped by scaffold family, RMSE in $\mathrm{p}K_i$ units and the two downstream models decided for both datasets, the DNN and SVM.

