In an antibody representation, as in a molecular fingerprint, the features that matter are few and buried among many that carry nothing: a language model's embedding of the whole sequence mixes the CDRs that vary with a framework that mostly does not. Many of the antibody representations in the pools were built for this thesis to separate the two (Table~\ref{tab:reps_antibodies}). On four antibody datasets the hybrid beats even the single representation that was best in hindsight, and on two of them that representation is one of ours (Table~\ref{tab:hybrid_vs_best_single}). On the anti-VEGF expression scan it is the CDR readout of ESM3 with the SVM, and on $\Delta\Delta G$ it is the mutation features with the SVM and the change from the parent embedding with the DNN.

