Three things hold for every result in this chapter. First, because of time and compute, most results are on the first outer fold only (Section~\ref{sec:method:evaluation}), and we give the fold count wherever more exist. Second, where a method has several settings, such as a share to delete or a strength, we report its best setting on the held-out score; because the single representation and the hybrid are picked the same way, every reported gain is optimistic. Third, the network's score changes from one fit to the next. On QM9 its second hybrid scores between 0.348 and 0.362 RMSE on the same fold and labels, depending on which experiment fitted it, whereas LightGBM gives one score in every experiment. A network gain of about 0.01 RMSE or less is inside that spread.

