Which detector selects the molecules to delete matters more than which action follows. We deleted the top 10\% by each of five detectors under the same hERG flips. The cliff-aware gap helped the hybrid most, then the GP, while the variance-head network, NGBoost and the heteroscedastic GP helped it least (Table~\ref{tab:noise:res:herg_flip_actions}). On the single representation the last three make things worse. The three that predict a spread from the features alone never read a label (Section~\ref{sec:noise:detection}), so they cannot see a flipped one. On LogD with outliers the GP was best for the network's hybrid (Table~\ref{tab:noise:res:logd_outlier_actions}). On a second fold of the hERG flips, none of the five improved the single representation, and only the cliff-aware gap improved the hybrid.

