A Gaussian process's own predicted spread plus its residual is the one model-uncertainty detector that could be graded. The other three are undefined under every damage kind that can be graded (Section~\ref{sec:noise:detection}). The GP was slightly ahead of the cliff-aware gap under outliers on Caco-2 and LogD, and behind it under every shift and every hERG flip kind (Additional file~\ref{app:add:noise_detect_other}). Detectors from outside cheminformatics did better than the residual where the residual is weakest. Under censoring the nearest-neighbor Shapley value reached 0.391 on Buchwald--Hartwig against 0.195 for the residual, and was also ahead on SMAC colloidal stability. Under the shift in 10\% the cleanlab score was well ahead of the residual on Buchwald--Hartwig. Each number is a mean over the detector's settings, and the Shapley value has many more settings than the residual.

